 "intro": "Spain and Africa, 210 to 202 BC. Hannibal has been in Italy for eight years. Your father and uncle have died fighting Carthage in Spain. You are Publius Cornelius Scipio, given command in Spain at twenty-five. Your war will take you from the walls of New Carthage to Hannibal himself at Zama.",
 "debrief": "Scipio took New Carthage in a day, sending men across the lagoon at low tide, and won the Spanish tribes by returning their hostages. At Ilipa he changed his battle line at dawn and drove Carthage from Spain. He made Masinissa his ally, invaded Africa against the Senate’s wishes, and burned the camps of Syphax and Hasdrubal near Utica. At Zama, lanes in his line let Hannibal’s elephants pass, and Masinissa’s cavalry returned to strike Hannibal’s veterans from behind. Carthage made peace, and Scipio was named Africanus. The other choices are what-ifs.",
